            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[**Sessions.** A new Sessions tab lists your Claude Code sessions across accounts, live and recently closed.

- A badge on the menu-bar icon counts the sessions waiting for you, and a notification tells you when one starts waiting.
- Click a session to bring its terminal to the front, or to reattach one whose window you closed.
- Sessions you launch from AgentMenu keep running when you close their window, and when you quit AgentMenu. Turn this off per folder with the `keep_running` preset field.
- Quit any live session from its row, or quit everything AgentMenu started with Quit all.
- Reopen all, or reopen the last one you closed. After a restart, AgentMenu offers to bring back what was running, and asks once whether to do that at every login.

**Updates install without a quit.** Before, a downloaded update waited for you to quit AgentMenu, which a menu-bar app rarely does. Now the popover shows **Restart to Update**, and AgentMenu restarts by itself after ten idle minutes. Your sessions survive the restart.

**Fixes**

- The popover no longer runs off the right edge of the screen when the menu-bar icon sits near it.
- The update window opens in front of the popover instead of behind it.
- A launch no longer cuts off a pending macOS Automation prompt.
]]></description>
